<rd-checkout class="lab wide rd-lab" aria-label="Two buyers, one blue mug">
  <div class="lab-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Interactive experiment</span></div>
  <h3>Two buyers, one blue mug</h3>
  <div class="lab-introduction">
    <p>A and B each want the last blue mug. Each transaction reads stock, attempts a stock change plus an order, then commits. The goal is to see whether the update rule lets both orders succeed.</p>
    <p class="try-this">Advance A once and B once so both read 1. Advance A to stage its write. Try B: it waits. Commit A, then finish B. Compare <strong>Write from earlier read</strong> with <strong>Guarded decrement</strong>. Use <strong>Roll back writer</strong> before a commit to discard its pending changes.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="lab-controls">
    <p class="lab-area-label">Controls</p>
    <div class="control-line"><label>Update rule <select data-policy><option value="unsafe">Write from earlier read</option><option value="guarded">Guarded decrement</option></select></label></div>
    <div class="control-line"><button data-buyer="A">Advance A</button><button data-buyer="B">Advance B</button><button data-abort disabled>Roll back writer</button><button data-reset>Reset</button></div>
  </div>
  <div class="lab-output paper-surface">
    <p class="lab-area-label">Result <span>Committed data and each transaction's pending work</span></p>
    <div data-view>
      <div class="lab-stats"><div><strong>1</strong><span>Committed stock</span></div><div><strong>0</strong><span>Committed orders</span></div><div><strong>None</strong><span>Write lock owner</span></div></div>
      <p>Both transactions are ready to read. No changes are pending.</p>
    </div>
    <p data-message role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">One blue mug remains. Both buyers have started a transaction.</p>
  </div>
  <details class="model-note"><summary>What this model leaves out</summary><p>This is a logical schedule based on PostgreSQL Read Committed behavior for one stock row. A write lock lasts until commit or rollback; ordinary reads see committed stock. Pending stock and order changes are grouped into one step. The guarded rule rechecks current stock after waiting; the unsafe rule uses its saved read. No real SQL runs. Disk recovery, replicas, deadlocks, timeouts, index work, and broader multi-row rules are omitted. Buttons advance statements, not measured time. The expected result is two orders under the unsafe schedule and one under the guarded schedule.</p></details>
  <noscript><p>The illustrated schedule produces two orders with the earlier-read rule even though stock ends at zero. A guarded decrement rejects the second purchase. Pending changes become visible only at commit.</p></noscript>
</rd-checkout>
<script>
  import { checkoutStart, checkoutStep } from '../../lib/explainers/rd-models.mjs';
  class RDCheckout extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      if (this.dataset.ready) return;
      this.dataset.ready = 'true';
      const policy = this.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-policy]')!;
      const abort = this.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-abort]')!;
      let state = checkoutStart(policy.value);
      const phase = { new: 'Ready to read', read: 'Ready to write', written: 'Ready to commit', committed: 'Committed', rejected: 'No stock; no order', aborted: 'Rolled back' };
      const render = () => {
        this.querySelector('[data-view]')!.innerHTML = `<div class="lab-stats"><div><strong>${state.stock}</strong><span>Committed stock</span></div><div><strong>${state.orders.length}</strong><span>Committed orders</span></div><div><strong>${state.lock || 'None'}</strong><span>Write lock owner</span></div></div><table class="rd-table"><caption>Transaction progress</caption><thead><tr><th>Buyer</th><th>Earlier read</th><th>Pending stock / order</th><th>Next step or outcome</th></tr></thead><tbody>${Object.entries(state.buyers).map(([b,t]) => `<tr><th>${b}</th><td>${t.read ?? '—'}</td><td>${t.staged === null ? 'None' : `${t.staged} / order ${b}`}</td><td>${phase[t.phase as keyof typeof phase]}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table><p class="rd-state ${state.orders.length > 1 ? 'rd-warning' : ''}">${state.orders.length > 1 ? 'Oversold: two orders claim the one mug.' : state.orders.length === 1 ? 'One committed order claims the mug.' : 'The mug has no committed order yet.'}</p>`;
        this.querySelector('[data-message]')!.textContent = state.message;
        abort.disabled = !state.lock;
        this.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-buyer]').forEach(b => { b.disabled = ['committed','rejected','aborted'].includes(state.buyers[b.dataset.buyer as 'A' | 'B'].phase); });
      };
      this.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-buyer]').forEach(b => b.addEventListener('click', () => { state = checkoutStep(state, b.dataset.buyer!); render(); }));
      abort.addEventListener('click', () => { if (state.lock) { state = checkoutStep(state, state.lock, 'abort'); render(); } });
      const reset = () => { state = checkoutStart(policy.value); render(); };
      policy.addEventListener('change', reset);
      this.querySelector('[data-reset]')!.addEventListener('click', reset);
      render();
    }
  }
  if (!customElements.get('rd-checkout')) customElements.define('rd-checkout', RDCheckout);
</script>
